From d7f5941cf35a92c1399065850bb2a34e15b0225f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:19:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 2/2] media: i2c: add Sony IMX616 sensor driver
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a V4L2 sub-device driver for the Sony IMX616, a 32MP Quad Bayer CMOS
image sensor on a 4-lane MIPI CSI-2 D-PHY interface. It is the front
camera of the Samsung Galaxy A52 4G (a52q, SM7125).

The driver exposes two binned modes (3264x2448 at 30 fps and 1632x1224
up to 120 fps) with exposure, analogue gain, flip, vblank/hblank and
test-pattern controls. The register tables were decoded from the vendor
CamX sensor module.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
